## 1. Executive Summary

The Hotel PMS is an integrated property, guest-services, point-of-sale, inventory and financial-management platform for a hotel operating approximately 120–200 rooms.

It will coordinate Front Office, reservations, room operations, restaurant and bar outlets, kitchen/KDS, laundry, gym, pool, transport, housekeeping, maintenance, procurement, inventory, customer management, employees, accounting and management reporting.

The central business principle is that departments can operate their own workflows and retain department-level reporting, while guest-related charges and financial transactions are consolidated through a shared billing and accounting foundation.

The first release should prioritize reliable room operations, reservations, check-in/check-out, guest folios, restaurant POS, charge-to-room, kitchen routing, users/permissions, configuration, auditability and deployment reliability. Additional departments will be added in controlled releases.

## 2. Product Vision and Objectives

### 2.1 Vision

Provide one reliable operational system through which hotel management can see and control rooms, guests, services, sales, stock, staff and financial performance.

### 2.2 Business objectives

- Reduce manual work and duplicate data entry.
- Maintain an accurate, real-time room inventory and room status.
- Consolidate eligible guest charges into a single folio.
- Preserve department-level revenue and cost visibility.
- Improve restaurant order fulfilment through KOT and KDS routing.
- Control stock across a central store and department stores.
- Strengthen cash, credit, discount, refund and approval controls.
- Produce auditable operational and financial reports.
- Support reliable operation over a local network.
- Allow growth in rooms, outlets, departments, users and properties without hardcoded limits.

### 2.3 Success measures

- No double-booking of the same room for overlapping confirmed stays.
- Every posted guest charge is traceable to its source department, source transaction and staff member.
- Every posted payment and accounting journal balances.
- Room status changes are visible to authorized users in real time.
- Inventory movements have a source, destination, quantity, unit and responsible user.
- Night audit can identify unresolved exceptions before closing a business date.
- Backup restoration is tested and documented.
- Critical workflows pass user acceptance tests before production rollout.

